### 3. Prevent Overflow in Validation (JournalBulkValidationService)
Because we used LongAdder to check for balance mismatches during the initial file upload, large mismatched batches would also slip through. Update runBalanceCheck to use AtomicReference.
**Find this inside runBalanceCheck:**
```java
ConcurrentHashMap<String, LongAdder> balanceMap = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

```
**Replace the aggregation logic with this:**
```java
        ConcurrentHashMap<String, AtomicReference<BigDecimal>> balanceMap = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
        // ... (Keep your Sets for seenCgls and duplicateCgls)

        // Pass 1
        rows.parallelStream().forEach(d -> {
            if (d.branch == null || d.currency == null || d.cgl == null || d.amount == null || d.txnType == null) return;
            
            // ... (Keep duplicate/presence tracking)

            BigDecimal val = d.amount;
            if ("Credit".equalsIgnoreCase(d.txnType) || "Cr".equalsIgnoreCase(d.txnType)) val = val.negate();
            
            String type = d.cgl.startsWith("5") ? "MEMO" : "NORMAL";
            String balKey = d.branch + "_" + d.currency + "_" + type;
            
            // Thread-safe BigDecimal addition without scaling or overflow risks
            balanceMap.computeIfAbsent(balKey, k -> new AtomicReference<>(BigDecimal.ZERO))
                      .updateAndGet(curr -> curr.add(val));
        });

        // Pass 2
        rows.parallelStream().forEach(d -> {
            if (d.branch == null || d.currency == null || d.cgl == null || d.amount == null || d.txnType == null) return;
            
            // ... (Keep Duplicate and Debit/Credit Presence Checks)

            String type = d.cgl.startsWith("5") ? "MEMO" : "NORMAL";
            String balKey = d.branch + "_" + d.currency + "_" + type;
            AtomicReference<BigDecimal> adder = balanceMap.get(balKey);

            synchronized (d.balErrors) {
                // ... (Keep Duplicate & Presence error adders)
                
                // Compare to exactly zero
                if (adder != null && adder.get().compareTo(BigDecimal.ZERO) != 0 && !d.balErrors.contains("Branch, Currency, and CGL-wise balance mismatch.")) {
                    d.balErrors.add("Branch, Currency, and CGL-wise balance mismatch.");
                }
            }
        });

```
With BigDecimal handling the math, the system can now perfectly aggregate numbers up to thousands of digits long without ever showing a negative sign or overflowing!
